    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n8762" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cŏāgŭlo</span></b> ,
			āvi, ātum (contr. COAGLAVI,
		Inscr. ap. <i><span class="en">Anthol. Lat. 1177</span></i> Meyer),
			1, v. a.
		coagulum, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to cause a fluid to curdle</i> or <i>coagulate</i> (mostly in the elder Pliny): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lac,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					12, 25, 54, § 123</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">20, 14, 53,
				§ 147</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">picem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					16, 11, 22, § 53</span></i>
			; v. Sillig <i>N. cr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					20, 23, 97, § 259</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sudorem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					35, 15, 52, § 186</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caseum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Pall. Mai, 9, 1 al.</span></i>
			</div>
